# Observer

Let an object announce that something happened, and let any number of listeners react, without the announcing object
knowing who they are.

## Use it when

- one event must trigger several independent reactions (update a display, raise an alarm, write a log);
- new reactions to the same event are expected, and today each one would mean editing the code that raises it;
- the reactions belong to other parts of the system, and the source should not depend on them.

## Do not use it when

- there is exactly one reaction and nothing suggests more: a direct call is clearer;
- the reactions must happen in a strict order with results that feed each other: that is a sequence of calls, or a
  pipeline;
- the "listener list" would always contain the same single object.

## Shape

```java
interface ReadingListener {
    void onReading(SensorReading reading);
}

final class WeatherStation {
    private final List<ReadingListener> listeners;           // received from outside
    WeatherStation(List<ReadingListener> listeners) { this.listeners = List.copyOf(listeners); }

    void record(SensorReading reading) {
        // … store the reading …
        for (ReadingListener listener : listeners) listener.onReading(reading);
    }
}

final class Display implements ReadingListener { /* show it */ }
final class FrostAlarm implements ReadingListener { /* only reacts below zero: the filter is its own */ }
final class History implements ReadingListener { /* keep it */ }

// the wiring of the application decides who listens
WeatherStation station = new WeatherStation(List.of(new Display(), new FrostAlarm(), new History()));
```

## Done right when

- the source only announces the event; it builds no reaction and names no listener;
- each reaction is its own listener, with its own rules about when to act;
- the reactions that existed before are listeners too, not direct calls next to the new ones;
- the list of listeners is assembled outside the source, where the application is wired;
- adding a reaction means one new listener and one line where they are registered.

## Usual mistakes

- One central class that receives the event and performs every reaction itself: the code moved, the coupling did
  not.
- The source still builds the content of some reactions and only delegates the others.
- The listener list is created inside the class that dispatches the events, so adding a listener still means editing
  it.
- Only some events go through listeners, and others are still handled by direct calls.

## Neighbors

- **Mediator**: coordinates objects that talk to each other in both directions; Observer is one-way.
- **Command**: when the reaction must be queued, retried or undone.
package hotel;

import hotel.messages.EmailSender;
import hotel.messages.SentMessages;
import hotel.reports.OccupancyReport;
import hotel.reports.RevenueReport;
import hotel.reservations.PriceCalculator;
import hotel.reservations.ReservationService;
import hotel.reservations.ReservationStore;
import hotel.rooms.Rooms;
import hotel.web.HttpApi;
import io.javalin.Javalin;

/** Puts the inn's pieces together and runs the HTTP server. */
public final class Hotel {

    private final Javalin server;

    public Hotel() {
        Rooms rooms = new Rooms();
        ReservationStore store = new ReservationStore();
        SentMessages sentMessages = new SentMessages();
        ReservationService reservations =
                new ReservationService(rooms, store, new PriceCalculator(), new EmailSender(sentMessages));
        HttpApi api = new HttpApi(
                rooms, reservations, sentMessages, new OccupancyReport(rooms, store), new RevenueReport(store));
        this.server = api.server();
    }

    /** Starts listening; port 0 picks a free port. Returns the port in use. */
    public int start(int port) {
        server.start(port);
        return server.port();
    }

    public void stop() {
        server.stop();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int port = Integer.parseInt(System.getenv().getOrDefault("PORT", "7070"));
        new Hotel().start(port);
    }
}
package hotel.reservations;

import hotel.documents.ReservationReceipt;
import hotel.messages.EmailSender;
import hotel.rooms.Room;
import hotel.rooms.Rooms;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

/** The life of a reservation: created, confirmed (paid), checked in, checked out, or cancelled. */
public final class ReservationService {

    static final String HOTEL_NAME = "Pousada Maré Alta";

    private final Rooms rooms;
    private final ReservationStore store;
    private final PriceCalculator priceCalculator;
    private final EmailSender emailSender;

    public ReservationService(
            Rooms rooms, ReservationStore store, PriceCalculator priceCalculator, EmailSender emailSender) {
        this.rooms = rooms;
        this.store = store;
        this.priceCalculator = priceCalculator;
        this.emailSender = emailSender;
    }

    public synchronized Reservation create(NewReservation request) {
        if (!request.checkOut().isAfter(request.checkIn())) {
            throw new HotelException(ErrorCode.INVALID_REQUEST, "check-out must be after check-in");
        }
        if (request.guests() < 1) {
            throw new HotelException(ErrorCode.INVALID_REQUEST, "a reservation needs at least one guest");
        }
        Room room = rooms.find(request.roomNumber())
                .orElseThrow(() -> new HotelException(
                        ErrorCode.ROOM_NOT_FOUND, "room " + request.roomNumber() + " does not exist"));
        if (request.guests() > room.capacity()) {
            throw new HotelException(
                    ErrorCode.CAPACITY_EXCEEDED,
                    "room " + room.number() + " takes at most " + room.capacity() + " guests");
        }
        boolean roomTaken = store.all().stream()
                .filter(existing -> existing.status() != ReservationStatus.CANCELLED)
                .anyMatch(existing -> existing.overlaps(room.number(), request.checkIn(), request.checkOut()));
        if (roomTaken) {
            throw new HotelException(
                    ErrorCode.ROOM_UNAVAILABLE, "room " + room.number() + " is taken on some of those nights");
        }
        Price price = priceCalculator.calculate(room, request.checkIn(), request.checkOut(), request.ratePlan());
        Reservation reservation = new Reservation(store.nextId(), request, price);
        store.save(reservation);
        return reservation;
    }

    public Reservation find(long reservationId) {
        return store.find(reservationId)
                .orElseThrow(() -> new HotelException(
                        ErrorCode.RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND, "reservation " + reservationId + " does not exist"));
    }

    /** The guest paid: the reservation is confirmed and the guest gets the receipt by e-mail. */
    public synchronized Reservation confirm(long reservationId) {
        Reservation reservation = find(reservationId);
        if (reservation.status() != ReservationStatus.PENDING) {
            throw notAllowed(reservation, "confirm");
        }
        reservation.confirmPayment();
        ReservationReceipt receipt = new ReservationReceipt(reservation, roomOf(reservation));
        emailSender.send(
                reservation.guest().email(),
                "Reserva confirmada - " + HOTEL_NAME,
                confirmationEmailBody(reservation, receipt));
        return reservation;
    }

    /**
     * Cancelling before the stay starts. What was paid comes back according to the rate plan (a pending
     * reservation was never paid, so nothing comes back).
     */
    public synchronized Reservation cancel(long reservationId) {
        Reservation reservation = find(reservationId);
        if (reservation.status() != ReservationStatus.PENDING
                && reservation.status() != ReservationStatus.CONFIRMED) {
            throw notAllowed(reservation, "cancel");
        }
        BigDecimal refund = switch (reservation.ratePlan()) {
            case STANDARD -> reservation.amountPaid();
            case NON_REFUNDABLE -> PriceCalculator.cents(BigDecimal.ZERO);
        };
        reservation.cancel(refund);
        return reservation;
    }

    public synchronized Reservation checkIn(long reservationId) {
        Reservation reservation = find(reservationId);
        if (reservation.status() != ReservationStatus.CONFIRMED) {
            throw notAllowed(reservation, "check in");
        }
        reservation.changeStatus(ReservationStatus.CHECKED_IN);
        return reservation;
    }

    /** The guest leaves: the stay is closed and the final receipt is handed over. */
    public synchronized ReservationReceipt checkOut(long reservationId) {
        Reservation reservation = find(reservationId);
        if (reservation.status() != ReservationStatus.CHECKED_IN) {
            throw notAllowed(reservation, "check out");
        }
        reservation.changeStatus(ReservationStatus.CHECKED_OUT);
        return new ReservationReceipt(reservation, roomOf(reservation));
    }

    /** A copy of the receipt, for a guest who lost it. Only paid reservations have one. */
    public ReservationReceipt receiptCopy(long reservationId) {
        Reservation reservation = find(reservationId);
        if (!reservation.isPaid()) {
            throw notAllowed(reservation, "issue a receipt for");
        }
        return new ReservationReceipt(reservation, roomOf(reservation));
    }

    private Room roomOf(Reservation reservation) {
        return rooms.find(reservation.roomNumber()).orElseThrow();
    }

    private static String confirmationEmailBody(Reservation reservation, ReservationReceipt receipt) {
        return "Olá, " + reservation.guest().name() + "!\n\n"
                + "Sua reserva na " + HOTEL_NAME + " está confirmada. Estes são os dados dela:\n\n"
                + receipt.text() + "\n"
                + "A entrada é a partir das 14h, e a saída, até as 12h.\n"
                + "Até breve!\n";
    }

    private static HotelException notAllowed(Reservation reservation, String operation) {
        return new HotelException(
                ErrorCode.OPERATION_NOT_ALLOWED,
                "cannot " + operation + " reservation " + reservation.id() + " while it is " + reservation.status());
    }
}
package hotel.reservations;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.time.LocalDate;

public final class Reservation {

    private final long id;
    private final int roomNumber;
    private final Guest guest;
    private final LocalDate checkIn;
    private final LocalDate checkOut;
    private final int guests;
    private final RatePlan ratePlan;
    private final Price price;
    private ReservationStatus status;
    private BigDecimal amountPaid;
    private BigDecimal refund;

    Reservation(long id, NewReservation request, Price price) {
        this.id = id;
        this.roomNumber = request.roomNumber();
        this.guest = request.guest();
        this.checkIn = request.checkIn();
        this.checkOut = request.checkOut();
        this.guests = request.guests();
        this.ratePlan = request.ratePlan();
        this.price = price;
        this.status = ReservationStatus.PENDING;
        this.amountPaid = PriceCalculator.cents(BigDecimal.ZERO);
    }

    public long id() {
        return id;
    }

    public int roomNumber() {
        return roomNumber;
    }

    public Guest guest() {
        return guest;
    }

    public LocalDate checkIn() {
        return checkIn;
    }

    public LocalDate checkOut() {
        return checkOut;
    }

    public int guests() {
        return guests;
    }

    public RatePlan ratePlan() {
        return ratePlan;
    }

    public Price price() {
        return price;
    }

    public ReservationStatus status() {
        return status;
    }

    /** What the guest paid: the total, once the reservation is confirmed; zero before that. */
    public BigDecimal amountPaid() {
        return amountPaid;
    }

    /** What the guest got back when the reservation was cancelled; null while it is not cancelled. */
    public BigDecimal refund() {
        return refund;
    }

    /** Confirmed, checked in or checked out: the guest paid and the room is theirs. */
    public boolean isPaid() {
        return status == ReservationStatus.CONFIRMED
                || status == ReservationStatus.CHECKED_IN
                || status == ReservationStatus.CHECKED_OUT;
    }

    /** The money the inn keeps from this reservation. */
    public BigDecimal amountKept() {
        return refund == null ? amountPaid : amountPaid.subtract(refund);
    }

    void changeStatus(ReservationStatus newStatus) {
        this.status = newStatus;
    }

    void confirmPayment() {
        this.status = ReservationStatus.CONFIRMED;
        this.amountPaid = price.total();
    }

    void cancel(BigDecimal refundAmount) {
        this.status = ReservationStatus.CANCELLED;
        this.refund = refundAmount;
    }

    boolean overlaps(int otherRoomNumber, LocalDate otherCheckIn, LocalDate otherCheckOut) {
        return roomNumber == otherRoomNumber
                && checkIn.isBefore(otherCheckOut)
                && otherCheckIn.isBefore(checkOut);
    }
}
package hotel.messages;

/** Sends e-mails to guests. Every e-mail sent is kept in the list of sent messages. */
public final class EmailSender {

    private final SentMessages sentMessages;

    public EmailSender(SentMessages sentMessages) {
        this.sentMessages = sentMessages;
    }

    public Message send(String to, String subject, String body) {
        return sentMessages.add("EMAIL", to, subject, body);
    }
}
package hotel.messages;

public record Message(long id, String channel, String to, String subject, String body) {
}
package hotel.messages;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

/** Every message the inn sent, so the front desk can check what each guest received. */
public final class SentMessages {

    private final List<Message> messages = new ArrayList<>();

    synchronized Message add(String channel, String to, String subject, String body) {
        Message message = new Message(messages.size() + 1L, channel, to, subject, body);
        messages.add(message);
        return message;
    }

    public synchronized List<Message> all() {
        return new ArrayList<>(messages);
    }
}
package hotel.documents;

import hotel.reservations.Reservation;
import hotel.rooms.Room;
import hotel.rooms.RoomType;
import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.time.LocalDate;

/** The receipt the guest gets when the reservation is confirmed, at check-out, and on request. */
public record ReservationReceipt(
        String title,
        long reservationId,
        String guestName,
        String guestCpf,
        int roomNumber,
        RoomType roomType,
        LocalDate checkIn,
        LocalDate checkOut,
        int nights,
        BigDecimal subtotal,
        BigDecimal discount,
        BigDecimal total) {

    public ReservationReceipt(Reservation reservation, Room room) {
        this(
                "Comprovante de reserva",
                reservation.id(),
                reservation.guest().name(),
                reservation.guest().cpf(),
                room.number(),
                room.type(),
                reservation.checkIn(),
                reservation.checkOut(),
                reservation.price().nights(),
                reservation.price().subtotal(),
                reservation.price().discount(),
                reservation.price().total());
    }

    public String text() {
        StringBuilder text = new StringBuilder();
        text.append(title).append(" nº ").append(reservationId).append('\n');
        text.append("Hóspede: ").append(guestName).append(" (CPF ").append(guestCpf).append(")\n");
        text.append("Quarto: ").append(roomNumber).append(" (").append(roomType).append(")\n");
        text.append("Entrada: ").append(TextFormat.date(checkIn))
                .append(" | Saída: ").append(TextFormat.date(checkOut))
                .append(" | ").append(nights).append(nights == 1 ? " diária" : " diárias").append('\n');
        text.append("Diárias: ").append(TextFormat.money(subtotal)).append('\n');
        if (discount.signum() > 0) {
            text.append("Desconto: ").append(TextFormat.money(discount)).append('\n');
        }
        text.append("Total: ").append(TextFormat.money(total)).append('\n');
        return text.toString();
    }
}
package hotel.documents;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter;
import java.util.Locale;

/** How money and dates are written in the texts the guest reads (Brazilian Portuguese). */
public final class TextFormat {

    private static final Locale BRAZIL = Locale.forLanguageTag("pt-BR");
    private static final DateTimeFormatter BRAZILIAN_DATE = DateTimeFormatter.ofPattern("dd/MM/yyyy");

    private TextFormat() {
    }

    public static String money(BigDecimal amount) {
        return "R$ " + String.format(BRAZIL, "%,.2f", amount);
    }

    public static String date(LocalDate date) {
        return BRAZILIAN_DATE.format(date);
    }
}
package hotel.reservations;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public record Price(int nights, BigDecimal subtotal, BigDecimal discount, BigDecimal total) {
}

